1
00:00:04,234 --> 00:00:07,549
Every decision makes waves. Ripple lets you see them before you decide.

2
00:00:07,549 --> 00:00:19,011
Ripple simulates 1,000 people. As you scroll, a year passes and opinions spread.

3
00:00:19,011 --> 00:00:22,980
Type any decision. Ripple reads it as you type.

4
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:30,451
It simulates 1,000 students, teachers and families, starting from real polls.

5
00:00:30,451 --> 00:00:37,600
Ripple suggests a narrower version and tests it by re-running the simulation.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,003
Phones only during class: 68% of adults support that in a Pew Research poll.

7
00:00:41,003 --> 00:00:46,126
Share a link that reproduces the exact result, or an image card.

8
00:00:46,126 --> 00:00:57,499
Watch the crowd make up its mind over a year.

9
00:00:57,499 --> 00:01:01,522
Hear what each group would say, in its own words.

10
00:01:01,522 --> 00:01:07,135
…and a town hall where the voices answer each other.

11
00:01:07,135 --> 00:01:14,340
Enter a ZIP code. Ripple builds the crowd from your district’s real Census data.

12
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:23,274
Then run the questions your town actually decides: parks, bond votes, school start times.

13
00:01:23,274 --> 00:01:29,713
Housing, school safety and climate start from real polls, with your neighbors in the room.

14
00:01:29,713 --> 00:01:33,244
27 real bills from Congress, updated every week from Congress.gov.

15
00:01:33,244 --> 00:01:40,254
Read what a bill does, see how far it got, and simulate it in your own district.

16
00:01:40,254 --> 00:01:46,153
Take it further: who decides, from Congress to your city council, and a letter that cites real polls.

17
00:01:46,153 --> 00:01:52,250
Ripple is a rehearsal. Send a 30-second survey to real people.

18
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:58,437
Real answers appear live next to Ripple’s prediction, group by group.

19
00:01:58,437 --> 00:02:05,258
Teachers can start a class. Students join with a code and a nickname, with no accounts.

20
00:02:05,258 --> 00:02:12,979
Everything students simulate and survey rolls up here, with how close the predictions were.

21
00:02:12,979 --> 00:02:24,276
Ripple also works in Spanish, including decisions typed in Spanish.

22
00:02:24,276 --> 00:02:31,861
It starts from the same real poll as the English version.

23
00:02:31,861 --> 00:02:39,774
Every number shows its source, and Ripple checks itself against 40 real polls.
